# auth.bug

> Module: auth (Kimlik Doğrulama) | Category: CORE  
> Last UI Tested: 02 June 2026

---

### B-AUTH-01: Google OAuth Login Button Not Visible

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Severity** | P3 — Low |
| **Status** | ⬜ **OPEN** |
| **Found** | UI testing — `/login` page has email/password form but NO Google OAuth button |
| **Bug** | The `auth.func` specification says the login page should have a "Google OAuth button (Google icon + 'Google ile Giriş Yap')". The actual login page has only email/password form and "Hesap Oluştur" link. Searched for "Google", "oauth", "gmail" in body — none found. |
| **Impact** | Users cannot sign in with Google accounts. Reduces signup conversion — many Turkish logistics professionals use Gmail. |
| **Root Cause** | The Google OAuth button may only render when `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` environment variable is set at build time. In the QA Docker environment, this variable might not be injected. |
| **Required Fix** | Verify `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` is passed as build arg in `docker-compose.qa.yml` or `.env.qa`. Alternatively, show the button with a disabled state when client ID is missing, so users know the feature exists. |
| **Files to Change** | `docker-compose.qa.yml` or `frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.tsx` |
| **CI Gate** | `production-integrity`: verify login page has Google button or disabled Google placeholder |
